      ":question/problem": "![](images/b8/b861fc99869649c19c117cf32fe13e19f7bee75d548c6fc08b68cde9faa7a8bc.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, the parallel lines $l$ and $m$ are crossed by the transversal $t$.\n\nConsider the following statement:\n\n> $m\u2220CAD = m\u2220FEH$\n\nThe table below gives the proof of the statement. Select the correct options in the table and thus complete the proof.\n\n|  | Statement | Reason |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| 1 | $\u2220CAD\u2245\u2220BAE$ | Vertical angles theorem |\n| 2 | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |\n| 3 | $\u2220CAD\u2245\u2220FEH$ | {{field-3}} |\n| 4 | $m\u2220CAD = m\u2220FEH$ | Definition of congruent angles |"
